From: Steven Enamakel <enamakel@tinyhumans.ai>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:31:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] docs(specs): document --env flag for run and score

Adds the repeatable `--env K=V` option to the `run` and `score` command
signatures and explains that it overrides `rsi.json`'s `env` for a single
invocation. The incumbent score cache is now keyed on `env` alongside the
revision and scorers, so a limited score can no longer stand in for a full one.

Auto-committed-on: macbook
Co-authored-by: Medulla <medulla@tinyhumans.ai>
---
 docs/specs/rsi-cli.md | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/specs/rsi-cli.md b/docs/specs/rsi-cli.md
index 564e032..6c2e2fe 100644
--- a/docs/specs/rsi-cli.md
+++ b/docs/specs/rsi-cli.md
@@ -208,8 +208,8 @@ is shown as `interrupted`.
 
 ```text
 tinyrsi check <loop>
-tinyrsi run   <loop> [--run ID] [--epochs N] [--port 8787] [--no-serve]
-tinyrsi score <loop> --label L [--checkout P]
+tinyrsi run   <loop> [--run ID] [--epochs N] [--port 8787] [--no-serve] [--env K=V]...
+tinyrsi score <loop> --label L [--checkout P] [--env K=V]...
 tinyrsi runs  [--loop NAME]
 tinyrsi show  <loop>/<run-id>
 tinyrsi serve [--port 8787]
@@ -222,6 +222,11 @@ replay then tail) and `/api/runs/<loop>/<run>/files/<path>` for `run.json`,
 `ledger.json`, an epoch's `brief.md` and a candidate's `change.diff`. The store
 layout is also what `apps/rsi-viz` discovers, with `RSI_RUN_ROOT=$TINYRSI_HOME`.
 
+`--env K=V` (repeatable) overrides `rsi.json`'s `env` for one invocation; `run`
+records the merged manifest in its frozen loop copy. The incumbent score cache
+is keyed on `env` as well as the revision and scorers, so a limited score never
+stands in for a full one.
+
 Exit status is 0 on success, 1 on a loop error, 2 on invalid input.
 
